# The Dry Sifter's block faces, plus the hashish item.
#
# PLACEHOLDER art. Warlon Mhite may redraw these; that is what the .mctex is for.
#
# Palettes are sampled from the mod's own existing textures, not invented, so the block sits next
# to hemp planks and hemp canvas without either looking out of place:
#
#   wood    from block/hemp_planks   (5A5236 .. A89D73)
#   canvas  from item/hemp_canvas    (262417 .. D6CB90)
#   resin   from item/decarboxylated_hemp, warmed towards blond for loose kief
#
# The side face is the crafting recipe read literally — plank frame, canvas screen through the
# middle, plank frame — which is also what the block is. Block faces are deliberately low contrast
# (vanilla blocks span a median 76 luminance steps against an item's 164); the hashish item is not.

@palette wood
. = none
1 = 3F3A26      seam, darker than any plank tone so the courses read
2 = 5A5236
3 = 67603E
4 = 82794E
5 = 8A8155
6 = 948A5E
7 = A1976C
c = 5F5A3B      canvas shadow
d = 827B4E      canvas midtone
e = A39C6A      canvas light
f = D6CB90      canvas highlight

# The screen itself — a plain weave seen through the open top, with the warp passing over the weft
# and back under it every two pixels. Each thread is two pixels wide but shaded across its width, so
# no 2x2 square is one flat colour; a mesh drawn as flat 2x2 blocks is an 8x8 drawing scaled up, and
# it moires badly the moment the block is more than a few metres away.
@texture block/sifting_box_screen 16x16 type=block tiling=true
edffedffedffedff
edccedccedccedcc
ffedffedffedffed
ccedccedccedcced
edffedffedffedff
edccedccedccedcc
ffedffedffedffed
ccedccedccedcced
edffedffedffedff
edccedccedccedcc
ffedffedffedffed
ccedccedccedcced
edffedffedffedff
edccedccedccedcc
ffedffedffedffed
ccedccedccedcced

@palette resin
. = none
1 = 4A3E1E      shadowed kief
2 = 6E5C2C
3 = 9A8140
4 = C0A257
5 = D9BC72      blond highlight — trichome heads catch the light
a = 241A0C      pressed hash, darkest
b = 3A2A12
c = 4E3818
d = 664A21
e = 7E5D2B

# Loose kief piling up on the screen. Granular, not smooth: the point is that it is a powder.
@texture block/sifting_box_kief 16x16 type=block tiling=true palette=resin
4534435445344353
3445354334453542
5343445453434454
4454533544545343
3534454335344535
4453345444533454
5345433453445345
3454554334554433
4533445455343454
5445353344435545
3354434545344334
4443545433455443
5534343454543354
3455454345334545
4345334533445434
5433455444353443

# Washed out in ice water instead of screened out dry. The SAME granular surface as the kief above,
# because it is the same trichome heads -- what ice-water buys is that there is almost no leaf in it,
# not a different substance. So this is that texture with the leaf-green muddiness taken out and a
# touch of wet sheen added, and nothing else. A palette that made it look like a different material
# would be claiming a potency difference the trade explicitly says colour does not predict.
@palette washed
b = 6B5A34      damp shadow between grains
c = 8E7A48
d = B29C63
e = D2BE8B      a wet grain catching the light
@texture block/sifting_box_bubble 16x16 type=block tiling=true palette=washed
